  "finding": "Differentiating the Green representation with the piecewise-constant traces of the discretisation gives a surface velocity that is exact for a boundary value without jumps and wrong by tens of percent for one that jumps at every panel edge. The relative error is unchanged by the data amplitude and by the quadrature order, and it does not vanish under refinement, because the O(h) error of the constant-panel potential is amplified to O(1) by the gradient. Building the same velocity from the exact identity grad(phi) = grad_tan(u) + n*q, with the tangential derivative recovered by a superconvergent least-squares patch fit, removes the amplification and converges at second order. The boundary integral equations are unchanged; only the post-processing of the surface velocity differs.",
